Why Catholics confess to a priest, and what other Christians say about it.","The Gospels were written long after Jesus by unknown authors, so they are legends.","This is the verse Protestant friends rightly stress.","Confession is the way of forgiveness, and the Church teaches that the sacrament is the ordinary form of it for grave sins.","The apostles saw and touched the Word made flesh, so what they saw can be depicted.","A question children ask, with this verse in the answer.","The memory verse of this lesson.","Fifth graders are preparing for deeper moral thinking and often for the Sacrament of Penance.","Sin is an offense against God and a wound to ourselves and others.","Matthew 23:9 forbids Catholics from calling priests “Father”.","All the baptized receive the Spirit and share in handing on the faith.","Heaven is just clouds and harps, or we simply float around as spirits.","Second reading on 2026-11-01","Second reading on 2027-04-25","First reading on 2028-01-03","John makes confession of the real incarnation the test of the Spirit, which later writers such as Ignatius applied against the Docetists.","John makes the confession of a real human nature, which Christ keeps, part of the test of faith.","Six- and seven-year-olds know the sting of being left out and the thrill of being in a group.","First reading on 2026-01-06","First reading on 2026-01-07","First reading on 2026-01-08","Second reading on 2026-06-12","First reading on 2027-01-06","First reading on 2027-01-07","First reading on 2028-01-06","All sins are equal in God’s eyes.","Not all sins are equal.","First reading on 2026-01-09","First reading on 2026-01-10","First reading on 2027-01-08","First reading on 2027-01-09","First reading on 2028-01-07","First reading on 2028-01-08"],"notes":[],"topics":["Confession and forgiveness of sins"],"r":{"1":[[0,9,9,90,0,-1,0],[1,1,3,80,1],[2,9,9,90,0,-1,0],[3,8,9,70,2],[4,9,9,90,0,-1,0],[5,9,9,70,3],[5,9,9,90,0,-1,0],[6,1,2,100,4],[7,9,9,60,5],[8,9,9,60,5],[9,9